test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:24:23:
   |
24 | unknown :: Files[p in nope] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                       ^
unknown name nope; name a value with #nope in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:26:31:
   |
26 | notList Path#ps :: Files[p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                               ^
ps is a Path, not a list, so p in ps can't pick elements of Files

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:28:33:
   |
28 | wrongKey Names#ps :: Files[p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                 ^
ps holds BranchName, but the key of Files is Path

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:30:35:
   |
30 | listOfLists Nest#ps :: Files[p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                   ^
ps holds Paths, but the key of Files is Path

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:32:45:
   |
32 | named OneAndAll(Path#p * Paths#ps) :: Files[p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                             ^
p is named twice in this transition

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:35:36:
   |
35 |   :: App(Files[p in ps] * Branches[b in bs]) -> App(Files[p in ps] * Branches[b in bs])
   |                                    ^
a transition picks several elements once; Files[p in ps] already does here

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:37:39:
   |
37 | targetOnly Paths#ps :: Files -> Files[p in ps](FileState.Conflicted)
   |                                       ^
Files[p in ps] picks elements only on the source side (or in a shared path); on the target, write Files[p]

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:39:47:
   |
39 | inGuard Paths#ps :: App => Mode.Idle // Files[p in ps](FileState.Conflicted) -> Mode.Busy
   |                                               ^
a guard can't pick elements with Files[p in ps]; write it on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:41:21:
   |
41 | unkeyed Paths#ps :: Plain[p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                     ^
Plain has no key, so [p in ps] can't pick elements; declare one, such as Plain = [FileState by Path]

